---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Research — A3S Labs" description="Applied machine learning, computer vision, data science and experimental systems from A3S Labs.">
  <section class="page-hero section-pad">
    <div class="shell page-hero-grid">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span>RESEARCH</span><span>A3S / 02</span></p>
      <div><h1>Models attached to real signals.</h1><p>Research work is most useful when it is reproducible, measurable and connected to an operational context.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad section-rule">
    <div class="shell research-list">
      <article class="research-item accent-honey"><div><span>01 / MULTIMODAL</span><h2>BeeUnity</h2></div><div><p>Queen-presence acoustic classification combined with climate, NDVI and hive-context modelling for bee-health intelligence.</p><a href="https://github.com/simlexx-k/QueenBeeAcoustics" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Repository ↗</a></div></article>
      <article class="research-item accent-violet"><div><span>02 / COMPUTER VISION</span><h2>Vesuvius surface detection</h2></div><div><p>Computer-vision experimentation around detecting and modelling surface structure from challenging image data.</p><a href="https://github.com/simlexx-k/vesuvius-surface-detection" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Repository ↗</a></div></article>
      <article class="research-item accent-cyan"><div><span>03 / DATA + ML</span><h2>Prediction and analysis</h2></div><div><p>A continuing body of work across exploratory analysis, classification, forecasting, graph methods, NLP and model evaluation.</p><a href="https://github.com/simlexx-k?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Browse work ↗</a></div></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad capability-band">
    <div class="shell capability-grid">
      <div class="capability-intro"><p class="section-kicker">Research standard</p><h2>Evaluation before decoration.</h2></div>
      <div class="capability-list">
        <article><span>A</span><div><h3>Reproducible pipelines</h3><p>Data preparation, model training, calibration and output generation should be traceable.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>B</span><div><h3>Conservative claims</h3><p>Model confidence is not ground truth; uncertain evidence stays uncertain.</p></div></article>
        <article><span>C</span><div><h3>Deployment path</h3><p>Useful research should have a route from notebook to API, interface or decision-support surface.</p></div></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
